# NotificationCard on DemoPage

## Source of truth
- Every sample is a real `NotificationCard` call from this project, including toasts.
- Copy the variant, icon, badge, slot, and classes. Every visible string is a `t()` call.
- The Show Code is the full `<NotificationCard>` a developer pastes. No comment-only stub and no `triggerNotification` payload in place of the tag.
- Same markup used twice (publish connect-X, purchase payment-fail) is shown once.
- Same look shown once: tip tokens/cash → one tip card; mint upload/submitted toasts → one upload success card.
- Slot CTAs use `DashboardPrimaryButton` — never a raw `<button>`.
- Description text goes through `NotificationCard` `:description` (renders `Paragraph` inside). Do not nest `Paragraph` in the slot.
- Long button style strings use `DashboardPrimaryButton` `theme` (e.g. `payoutFail`, `tipLimitAction`). Long card looks use `NotificationCard` `theme` (e.g. `payoutFail`, `tipSuccess`, `tipLimit`).
- Tip success / tip limit: use `theme="tipSuccess"` / `theme="tipLimit"` — no `#icon` / `#default` template markup and no ibb URLs in Show Code. Icons come from the asset map inside the card.

## Do not demo
- Invented variants, “learn more” links, or demo-only sentences that no page renders.
- `TopUpStep1.vue` — it imports the component and never renders it.
- Duplicate tip cash vs tokens, or duplicate mint success-teal upload toasts.
